      "writtenOn": "2020-09-14T20:37:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I\u0027m similarly wary. It seems straightforward that CONFIG_USB_PD_VBUS_MEASURE_CHARGER would indicate we can measure Vbus through the charger, but since that config is used so little in the codebase I\u0027m not sure how well tested it is for the boards that use it. \n\nSo I think for now we\u0027ll keep this at the board level for now.  We\u0027ll revisit as boards move to TCPMv2 I imagine, since not all of them will have a good TCPCI rev 2.0 chip to give vSafe0V, and as far as I can tell a good vSafe0V really improves our PR swap behavior.",
